<header><p class="enc-kicker"><a href="/encyclopedia/conflicts/20th-century">Conflicts &amp; Resolutions</a> · Battle</p><h1 class="enc-title">Battle of Passchendaele</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1917">1917</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a> · Also known as Third Battle of Ypres · Part of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/first-world-war">First World War</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Battle of Passchendaele, or Third Battle of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ypres">Ypres</a>, was a British-led offensive on the Western Front in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/belgium">Belgium</a> from July to November 1917. Fought in heavy rain over ground churned into mud by shelling, it gained only a few miles before Canadian troops took the ridge and village of Passchendaele, at a cost of hundreds of thousands of casualties on both sides.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/battle-of-passchendaele.jpg" alt="Battle of Passchendaele" width="320" height="245" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Frank Hurley · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Chateauwood.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
